[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one issue, one fix queued. Read the reports instead of
the subject lines and the ticket holds three problems. Each one now has a ticket of its own.

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

<Callout kind="warn">
The queued parser fix closes only <code>parser</code>. The other two keep coming in after it ships.
</Callout>

## The three problems

**`parser`: the shared parser reads dates month first.** Every tenant in #4471 writes the day
first, so a booking for 7 April goes out for 4 July. It reaches them through the app, by email,
and through booking-v2's form.

**`hint`: booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field.** People at day-first tenants on
booking-v3 type what the hint tells them, month first, and the form reads it day first. Same
swap, different bug: only the form, only booking-v3. The parser fix does not touch it; the hint
or the form's reading has to change.

**`one-day`: the date moves by one day.** "Tuesday 12 May" shows as "Monday 11 May"; a client in
Lisbon gets Tuesday and one in Toronto gets Monday. Nothing is swapped. That points to a time
zone (a date stored as midnight in one zone, shown in another), not to the parser. The desk had
listed these in `desk-notes.json` and footnoted them under `parser`; here they count apart.

## How the reports were split

- One id, one report: the export pages overlap, and the ids that come twice are dropped.
- The tenant decides, not intake's tag. `meta.intakeTag` is a guess from the reporter's browser;
  the cause comes from the tenant's locale and booking form (`causes.ts`). The two disagree, and
  the *tagged as* column shows by how much.
- A report the desk read as a one-day move is `one-day`, whatever its tenant.
- Checked against the bodies: every body that names two dates has them day and month swapped
  (`parser`, `hint`) or one day apart (`one-day`). The few that name no dates stay with their
  tenant's cause.

## Lessons

- A subject line says what the reporter saw, not what broke. Merging on it put three bugs in one
  ticket ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)).
- Count by the tenant, not by intake's tag.
- A footnote under a cause is a problem without a ticket.

